Create one reusable, text-free popup panel frame for the Urkaaaz match-result
screen. It is shared by Victory and Defeat; do not bake outcome-specific
colors, illustrations, rewards, labels, or controls into this asset.

## References

- Attach `match_result_victory.png` and `match_result_defeat.png` as
  composition references. Use their shared dark wood/iron panel, framed
  Green Frontier illustration window, warm metal edging, and restrained
  hardware as visual guidance.
- Use `loadout_header_frame.png` only as a secondary reference for the
  established Urkaaaz wood, metal, lighting, and material finish.
- The mockups are flattened screen compositions. Do not reproduce their
  battlefield, characters, text, buttons, coin artwork, or other UI content
  in this panel asset.

## Output

- Generate exactly one isolated transparent PNG:
  `match_result_popup_panel.png`.
- Canvas: 2400 x 1680 px, RGBA, rendered at 4x the target 600 x 420 dp size.
- Preserve a 10:7 landscape proportion. The panel must scale uniformly and
  remain legible when rendered smaller than its target dp size.
- Save the review asset under `assets_src/match/result-ui/`.
- Keep the area outside the panel transparent. The game renders the
  battlefield behind the popup and applies its dimming overlay in UI.

## Shared panel structure

- Build one substantial dark wood-and-iron backing with a clear outer
  silhouette, warm bronze/gold metal edging, restrained corner plates, and
  readable depth. Match the shared framing language of both mockups.
- Include a wide, centered illustration window in the upper-middle area.
  Render its inner opening fully transparent so the runtime can place a
  separate Victory or Defeat illustration behind the frame.
- Frame the illustration opening with a continuous inset border. Keep the
  opening rectangular and unobstructed; do not place ornaments over the
  visible art area.
- Reserve a small centered top plaque area for the dynamic level/biome line.
  It may have a dark inset surface and metal trim, but must contain no text.
- Leave a broad, calm dark panel surface below the illustration window for
  optional reward content and native UI controls. Do not draw fixed rows,
  separators, or placeholders there; the runtime must be able to omit
  unavailable rewards without leaving an empty baked-in row.
- Keep the central upper edge clear for a separate, outcome-specific title
  plaque to overlap the frame. Do not include a victory laurel, red defeat
  plate, or result title in this shared asset.
- Ensure the panel has enough unobstructed interior space for live UI text
  and the gold, dark, or red button backgrounds to be layered independently.

## Visual direction

- Follow the mockups' polished fantasy-game finish: dark, warm wood; deep
  iron surfaces; bronze/gold bevels; controlled highlights; and subtle
  handcrafted detail.
- Keep the panel visually strong over a dimmed battlefield without
  overpowering the separately rendered result illustration or labels.
- Keep materials and lighting neutral enough to work with both the warm-gold
  Victory treatment and restrained ember-red Defeat treatment.
- Use symmetrical corner hardware and even safe margins. Avoid fragile,
  tiny details that disappear when the panel is scaled down.
- Render no shadows or glow outside the transparent canvas bounds.

## Runtime separation

- This asset is only the reusable popup backing and illustration-window
  frame. Android renders the live outcome title, level/biome context, reward
  data, icons, and button labels separately.
- Victory and Defeat use the same panel asset and geometry. Their separate
  title plaques and illustrations are layered by the UI.
- The runtime may hide all reward content when no reward is available; the
  panel must not imply that a gold reward or unlock exists.
- Do not include any button face; the UI uses the existing gold/red families
  and the separately generated dark button family.

## Negative prompt

text, letters, numbers, words, labels, title, logo, watermark, signature,
character, unit, catapult, landscape, battlefield, sky, grass, leaves, coins,
reward icon, unlock icon, button, button label, gold amount, victory wreath,
defeat emblem, red outcome treatment, full-screen background, screenshot,
phone frame, presentation board, opaque exterior, opaque illustration
window, ornaments across the window, excessive glow, asymmetrical hardware,
cropped frame, clipped corners

## Review checklist

- Confirm exactly one 2400 x 1680 RGBA PNG exists with the specified name.
- Confirm pixels outside the panel silhouette are transparent.
- Confirm the illustration-window opening is fully transparent and large
  enough for the separate landscape illustration.
- Confirm the top plaque is blank and leaves room for a live level/biome line.
- Confirm the panel has no fixed reward row or control artwork.
- Confirm the central upper edge can accept separate Victory and Defeat title
  plaques without covering the illustration opening.
- Preview the frame over both match-result mockups at the target size and
  verify that its shared neutral material treatment suits both outcomes.
